<title>THAILAND: S&amp;P says sees Thai interest rates staying high.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says sees Thai interest rates staying high.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai interest rates will remain high and continue to squeeze corporate performance, U.S. rating agency Standard &amp; Poor's (S&amp;P) said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't expect any easing in interest rates and that continues to negatively impact on already stressed borrowers,&quot; Peter Sikora, associate director of S&amp;P's financial institutions ratings group, told Reuters Financial Television.</p>
<p>Thai borrowing rates are already among the highest in the region with the minimum lending rate at around 13.75 percent.</p>
<p>S&amp;P last week placed several Thai ratings under negative review as the country's economy deteriorates.</p>
</text>
